    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Speaking and interaction practice",
    "subtitle": "A room that works · 1",
    "context": "Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to compare arrangements for a living space and resolve a practical problem.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U3-03-required-speaking-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Explain the situation",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U3-03-required-speaking-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "spoken",
            "prompt": "A room that works · 1: Explain the practical problem and your proposed response to an absent partner. State one constraint or condition and explain how it changes the plan.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "学校让我们找一个房间一起看书。我和朋友先去一楼，门口写着今天有人上课，不能进去。我们又上二楼，发现一个开着门的房间。\n\n房间里没有人，桌子上放着几本书，桌子旁边有三把椅子。我以为这里也有人用，想再去一个房间。朋友说先问老师。\n\n老师告诉我们，书是给来这里看书的人看的，不是谁把东西忘在这里。我们可以坐下看，也可以看自己拿来的书。\n\n我们坐在桌子旁边，朋友看自己拿来的书，我看桌子上的一本。过了一会儿，同学来问还有没有椅子，我说旁边这把没有人坐，他就坐下了。\n\n三个人都找到可以坐的椅子，也都可以看书。走的时候，我们把书放回桌子上，没有带走。下次有人来，也可以在这里坐下看书。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Take your speaking turn",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed speaking practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "My problem and proposed response follow the source."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "I connected a real condition or constraint to the result."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
    ],
